Prepare the demonstration – Organize the project, presentation, screenshots, and required equipment.

Introduce the project – Explain the problem, objectives, and purpose of the project.

Explain the methodology – Describe the major phases, technologies, and methods used.

Demonstrate the system – Show the actual working features of the project step by step.

Present the results – Explain the outcomes and how the project meets the requirements.

Answer questions – Respond to questions and clarify doubts from the audience.

Collect feedback – Gather suggestions and comments for possible improvements.

Discuss future enhancements – Explain additional features or improvements that could be added later.
